[0,"o","\r\u001b[1;34m\u001b[0m                                                                                                                        \u001b[1;34m########################################################################################################################\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m    Exercise: Backing Up /etc Nightly\u001b[0m                                                                                   \u001b[1;34m        Requirements\u001b[0m                                                                                                    \u001b[1;34m          Hosts: servera, with workstation holding the offsite copy\u001b[0m                                                     \u001b[1;34m          Back up /etc every night at 10 p.m., as root\u001b[0m                                                                  "]
[0.000024,"o","\u001b[1;34m          Copy each snapshot to workstation as an offsite copy\u001b[0m                                                          "]
[0.000036,"o","\u001b[1;34m          servera is always on, so a system crontab is the right home\u001b[0m"]
[0.000009,"o","                                                   "]
[0.000009,"o","\u001b[1;34m        Tasks\u001b[0m"]
[0.000048,"o","                                                                                                           \u001b[1;34m          1. Write the backup script on servera\u001b[0m"]
[0.000028,"o","                                                                         "]
[0.000026,"o","\u001b[1;34m          2. Schedule it in /etc/cron.d\u001b[0m"]
[0.000007,"o","                                                                                 "]
[0.000026,"o","\u001b[1;34m          3. Find out why nothing happened\u001b[0m"]
[0.000014,"o","                                                                              "]
[0.000143,"o","\u001b[1;34m          4. Confirm root ran it, then set the real 10 p.m. schedule\u001b[0m                                                    \u001b[1;34m          5. Clean up the schedule, script, and offsite copies\u001b[0m                                                          \u001b[1;34m########################################################################################################################\u001b[0m"]
